---
import ItemPage from '../../layouts/ItemPage.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much is a Cookie Dough Blizzard at Dairy Queen?', a: 'It typically costs about $3.49 for a Mini, $4.49 for a Small, $5.49 for a Medium and $6.49 for a Large. Prices vary by location.' },
  { q: 'How many calories are in a Cookie Dough Blizzard?', a: 'About 410 calories for a Mini, 590 for a Small, 800 for a Medium and 1,180 for a Large.' },
  { q: 'Is the cookie dough in the DQ Blizzard raw?', a: 'No. The cookie dough pieces are made to be eaten as they are, without raw eggs, so they are safe to eat frozen.' },
  { q: 'Is the Cookie Dough Blizzard available all year?', a: 'Yes. It is one of Dairy Queen’s year-round Blizzard flavors.' },
];
---
<ItemPage
  title="DQ Cookie Dough Blizzard: Price & Calories (2026)"
  description="Cookie Dough Blizzard prices: Mini $3.49, Small $4.49, Medium $5.49, Large $6.49. Calories by size, what is in it and how it compares to Oreo."
  name="Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough Blizzard"
  category={{ name: 'Blizzard Treats', href: '/categories/blizzard-treats' }}
  image="/Images/cookie-dough-blizzard.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough Blizzard"
  badges={['Year-round', 'A top-3 favorite']}
  quick="A Cookie Dough Blizzard at Dairy Queen costs about $3.49 for a Mini, $4.49 for a Small, $5.49 for a Medium and $6.49 for a Large. A Small has about 590 calories. It is on the menu year-round. Prices vary by location."
  from="From $3.49"
  intro="Soft chocolate chip cookie dough pieces and fudge blended into vanilla soft serve. Where the Oreo Blizzard is crunchy, this one is chewy and buttery, and it is one of the most ordered flavors after Oreo."
  spec={[
    ['Inside', 'Vanilla soft serve, cookie dough pieces, fudge'],
    ['Sizes', 'Mini · Small · Medium · Large'],
    ['Calories (Small)', '590'],
    ['Availability', 'Year-round'],
  ]}
  allergens="Milk, Wheat, Soy, Eggs"
  table={{
    title: 'Cookie Dough Blizzard price and calories by size',
    head: ['Size', 'Price', 'Calories'],
    rows: [['Mini', '$3.49', '~410'], ['Small', '$4.49', '590'], ['Medium', '$5.49', '800'], ['Large', '$6.49', '1,180']],
  }}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Cookie Dough vs. Oreo Blizzard</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Cookie Dough</th><th><a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Small price</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Large price</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$6.49</td><td class="price-cell">$5.99</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Small calories</strong></td><td>590</td><td>420</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Texture</strong></td><td>Soft and chewy</td><td>Crunchy</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Taste</strong></td><td>Buttery and sweet</td><td>Chocolate cookie, less sweet</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Can’t decide? Ask for half Oreo and half cookie dough in one Blizzard. It is one of the best-known <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-secret-menu">DQ secret menu</a> combos.</p>

  <h2>Ordering tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It is filling. A Mini (about 410 calories) is a good size after a meal.</li>
    <li>Want it for a party? The <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard-cake">Cookie Dough Blizzard Cake</a> serves 12 to 16.</li>
    <li>See how it ranks against every other flavor in our <a href="/blog/best-blizzard-flavors-ranked">Blizzard rankings</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</ItemPage>
